# App layout

Every app in this repo is one tree. `main.ts` is the `serve()` callback and
boots it. Feature folders export a `Group` from `mod.ts` (`mod.tsx` when the
file contains JSX). `/` and one-offs such as `staticFile` live on the root
group; every other page is a prefixed feature group. README snippets may
inline `serve(callback)` to show the whole flow; those are not apps.

## File names

Deno snake_case. Feature folders match the path (`slow_write/` for
`/slow-write`). Layout and middleware files are `{folder}_{role}`:
`menu_layout.tsx`, `menu_middleware.ts`. Nested `reviews/` uses
`reviews_layout.tsx`. At the app root: `root_layout.tsx`,
`logger_middleware.ts`, `errors.tsx`. Client modules are `*_client.ts`
(`clock_client.ts`) and sit beside the file that registers them. No `routes/`
directory, no app `client/` folder, and no `_` magic prefixes.

`errors.tsx` holds the named `notFound`, `error`, and `errorFallback`
exports. Those are not routes. Root `notFound` / `error` live on the root
callback; a feature group's `notFound` / `error` live on that group's `mod.ts`.
`errorFallback` stays on `serve()` options.

Ordinary extra modules (`todos.ts`, later `db.ts`) sit beside the handlers.
No blessed view / service / DAL layer: extract `menu_service.ts` or a
component when needed. No `layouts/` or `middleware/` folders.

## Exports

A component that returns `Element` is PascalCase (`Home`, `RootLayout`,
`ErrorPage`). Middleware and per-method handlers are camelCase (`logger`,
`list`, `add`).

`mod.ts` is the controller for that group: `group()` plus handlers (inline or
named functions in the same file). No `*_route.tsx` and no `controller.ts`
inside a feature folder. Root `/` and one-off probes are `*_route.ts(x)`:
they export handlers only, and only the root table in `main.ts` imports from
them.

## Table

`main.ts` is the `serve()` callback. It binds `route("/")`, imported Groups,
and any root one-offs, then calls `serve`. Feature folders import `group`
from `dashi` at module scope and export the `Group`. The parent drops that
value into `routes`. Do not `import { group }` inside a bag callback. Do not
export `route()`.

Every feature is a group, including one-page features:

```ts
import { group } from "dashi";

export const menu = group("/menu", ({ route }) => ({
  layouts: [MenuLayout],
  routes: [route("/", { GET: Menu })],
}));
```

`group("/", …)` is illegal. Pathless `group(({ route }) => …)` is only a
layout/middleware shell with no extra prefix, still exported from a file.
Nested folders are nested groups. A pre-built `Group` types `ctx.params` from
its own prefix; nested groups do not read ancestor params they did not
declare. Shared data goes on `ctx.state`.

`main.ts` is:

```ts
import { serve } from "dashi";
import { Home } from "./home_route.tsx";
import { RootLayout } from "./root_layout.tsx";
import { errorFallback } from "./errors.tsx";
import { menu } from "./menu/mod.ts";

if (import.meta.main) {
  serve(({ route }) => ({
    layouts: [RootLayout],
    routes: [route("/", { GET: Home }), menu],
  }), { errorFallback });
}
```

## Fixtures

The main fixture (`int-tests/fixtures/app/`) matches this layout. Extra
fixtures that cannot share that `serve()` table are a small `main.ts` or
`main.tsx` in their own folder, inline `serve(callback)` harnesses. They are
not workspace members. The e2e fixtures use the same tree; extra e2e fixtures
follow the same rule.

## Imports

App code imports from `dashi`. `dashi/jsx-runtime` is the Deno
`jsxImportSource` subpath, not a second public import style. The public vs
internal export list and the JSR `exports` map stay COO-27.
